.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.ad l
.TP
\fBcheck\fR
.ad l
Reports whether this machine is exposed. Read-only. Most tools run it when you give no command; the PHP2Shell and eMudhra mitigation scripts apply their protection instead, so type the command every time.
.TP
\fBhunt\fR
.ad l
Looks for signs of exploitation. Read-only.
.TP
\fBmitigate\fR
.ad l
Applies protection you can undo. Copies every file first, checks the result with the service's own checker, puts the original back if the check fails, and reloads nothing unless you ask. Supports \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR.
.TP
\fBrollback\fR
.ad l
Undoes what mitigate changed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.ad l
.TP
\fBSCAN_CONTAINERS\fR
.ad l
Set to 0 to skip running docker and podman containers.
.TP
\fBSTATE_DIR\fR
.ad l
Where a tool keeps its backups and rollback record. Each tool documents its default under /var/lib/psf\-security\-patches.
.SH FILES
